  ↳ 4:## TL;DR — where this leaves the question (readable as an email) (+8 lines)
I ran the probes campaign wake. Three findings got stronger, but the "route then densify" probe (re-compress the page the model picks at twice the slots) failed its safety check. I fixed the code; it gets re-checked next wake. The only thing you might want to change is the campaign's 60-cell cap.

**Why I was woken:** the flagged error was a cluster preemption (my job was bumped and automatically re-queued). That is a known, harmless issue.

**New results** (judge accuracy ↑ = share of answers the judge model accepts; 1,500 questions per cell unless noted):

| Probe | Result vs its baseline | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Answer passages compressed together, on the older "tail" slot-layout model | .627 vs .569, +.058 [+.035, +.082] | One model only, so provisional; the gain does not need the newer layout |
| No answer labels: the 3 passages the model's own attention ranks first, compressed together | .614 vs .582, +.032 [+.009, +.056] | Meets its +.03 gate at seed 42; seed-43 repeat running |
| Same with the top 2 passages | .612 vs .582, +.030 | At the gate's edge |
| Keep only the half of the slots the decoder attends to most (slot = one compressed vector, 1 per 8 tokens), documents, seed 43 | .615 vs .615, +.000 [−.009, +.009] | Same tie as seed 42; the gate's last piece (the blind-half cell) is running |

**Route then densify:**
- **Safety check failed:** at the normal compression rate, the new code should reproduce the plain answers. It matched only 233 of 300 (the rule needs 97%), even though the slot count was identical.
- **Likely cause:** the code re-compressed the picked page on its own. The normal path compresses all four pages together in one batch. That changes the page's numbers slightly, and image answers are known to flip on tiny numeric changes.
- **What I did:** cancelled the two full cells before they started. I changed 9 lines so the page is re-compressed inside its usual batch, which should reproduce the plain slots exactly. The fix compiles, but its tests have not run yet. The next wake runs all the checks in one job, under the same rules. The full cells go only if it passes.

**Also done:**
- I fixed the claims the automatic checker flagged in the state file. For example, I removed "half noise", because the seed-42 value on today's code is still being measured.
- I built the TextVQA set with its OCR text (500 rows, all 500 questions matched). The gold answer appears word for word in the OCR text on 60% of rows.
- I corrected a wrong note: `eval_mm_4b.sh` and the other launchers are already tracked by git, so nothing needs force-adding.
- Still running: evidence-then-answer (seed 42), int8 slot storage (seed 43), the blind-half seed-43 cell, keeping only a quarter of the slots, slot pruning on photos, the seed-43 no-oracle repeat, and the one-chunk-of-ten re-run.

**Budget:** 57 of the 60 campaign cells are used (every submitted job counts, including the two I cancelled). The last 3 go to the route-then-densify checks and its two full cells. So the TextVQA text-only cell and the seed-43 evidence-then-answer repeat will not run.

Decision for you: raise the cell cap by 3 if you want the TextVQA text-only cell, the seed-43 evidence-then-answer repeat and one spare relaunch. Otherwise nothing is needed from you.
